Expand at small $\epsilon$: $S_0(\epsilon)
  =
  \frac{1}{\epsilon}
  -\frac12
  +\frac{\epsilon}{12}
  -\frac{\epsilon^3}{720}
  +O(\epsilon^5).$ The board obtains this by expanding numerator and denominator separately, factoring one power of $\epsilon$, and then expanding the reciprocal. That calculation contains several in-class sign checks; the compact expression  is its cleaned result.

